2026-06-13 feat/dim-player-team-season — CPO ruling on object classification (PR A of the player-model redesign). The iteration-2 scope-auditor FAILed: per layering.md's dimension-qualification rules, dim_player_team_season does not earn dim_ status — it is a conformed many-to-many RELATIONSHIP (player↔team↔season rostered membership), not an entity, and it is attribute-less (the "degenerate dimension" pattern the rules exclude). layering.md recognizes only dim_ (entities) and fct_ (events); no category exists for a relationship/mapping table, and there is no precedent in 3_core. CPO design-session findings (2026-06-13): the conformed reusable mapping is a CORE concern (layering.md 3_core owns "relationship logic... that marts/intermediate reuse rather than re-derive"); base cannot host it (base may not be the system of record and cannot ref the core dim_competition_season needed to resolve season_sk).
  CPO RULING (2026-06-13): the model name should reflect WHERE it sits (core), so KEEP the dim_ prefix AND add a _mapping suffix → final name `dim_player_team_season_mapping` (dim_ = core home; _mapping = it is a relationship table, not an entity). ADJUST layering.md's rules to recognize a conformed relationship/mapping table as a valid dim_ — exempt from the Entity condition and the degenerate-dimension exclusion, still required to satisfy Reuse + Conformance, declare its relationship grain, and test grain uniqueness; grain is one row per association occurrence (many rows per participating entity). Add layering.md to the task scope (amendment) + inventory row. Exact rule wording to be confirmed before the gated commit.

