  commit gate and the CI recompute produce DIFFERENT `diff_sha256` values for provably identical
  commits (`git ls-remote` confirms both sides hold the same two SHAs). Five candidate bases, the
  commit count, line endings and local git config were each ruled out BY MEASUREMENT, not by
  reasoning — the evidence table is on GitLab #63. Root cause: both sides hash the RENDERED PATCH
  TEXT, a presentation format whose bytes depend on git version, platform and diff settings.
  Demonstrated on one machine with identical commits: the same content hashes to `0c1ef8af` at
  `-U3` and `ca1afb7d` at `-U0`.

